`xfire_ids.json`: Rekindle game database id -> Xfire game id (plan E7.2 "Game icons").

Provenance
  Imported by `cargo xtask import-xfire-data` (plan E7.7.3) from the project owner's
  Xfire install tree, git commit ba066924 ("xfire re'd"; removed from the tree by
  5a20b508), restored into the git-ignored `legacy/unpacked/`:
    legacy/unpacked/xfire_games.ini  BLAKE3 e07ee92fc304a5947e10895b3e33f387737d7246dc89736584a5c4d72c2c5e90

Licence
  This is Xfire, Inc. content; Xfire is defunct. The project owner ruled on 2026-10-15
  that Xfire's own assets may be used in Rekindle. Rekindle's MIT LICENSE does not cover
  it.

How it was made
  Each `default_games.json` game is matched by name and process: an Xfire game whose
  `LongName` equals the game's name (letters and digits, case folded) and whose
  `LauncherExe` or `DetectExe` is one of its process names. 15 of the database's games
  match; the rest keep their slug icon.
    4102 Dota 2 -> 6957
    4180 Counter-Strike: Global Offensive -> 7186
    4181 Counter-Strike 2 -> 8507
    4300 Minecraft -> 6216
    4400 Fortnite -> 8508
    4500 Overwatch 2 -> 8546
    4501 World of Warcraft -> 4216
    5001 Stardew Valley -> 8587
    5002 Terraria -> 6613
    5100 The Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim -> 6984
    5101 Starfield -> 8519
    5400 Path of Exile -> 6885
    5500 Cyberpunk 2077 -> 8548
    5601 Warframe -> 7785
    5701 Phasmophobia -> 8535
